   231	Since g̃₂ lies beyond h̃, the path ⟨g̃₁g̃₂⟩ runs g̃₁ → Ũ → h̃ → … → g̃₂ and
   232	therefore contains q̃.  Apply Lemma 2.12 at ã := q̃.  Then
   233	`Q₁ = br_q̃(g̃₁)`, `Q₂ = br_q̃(g̃₂) = br_q̃(h̃)`, and Q₃ is precisely the union
