   473	## 7. Consequence paragraph for the campaign soundness ledger
   474	
   475	**Effect on DOMRINA-II-SOUNDNESS.**  The charged replay withheld promotion of
   476	DOMRINA-II-SOUNDNESS on exactly two grounds, both root-location gaps in the
   477	first half.  Both are now repaired: Corollary 3.8 b) in full, and Lemma 3.15
   478	in the conclusion that was charged, with a named and characterised residual in
   479	its companion inessentiality clause at a single fork vertex.  The correct
   480	ledger move is therefore narrow and should be stated narrowly:
   481	`DOMRINA-II-FIRST-HALF-ROOT-LEDGER = CLOSED`, and, combining with the replay's
   482	already-typed `LEMMA 3.12 = REPAIRED`, `LEMMA 3.13 = REPAIRED`,
   483	`LEMMA 3.14 = REPAIRED`, the disposition
   484	`DOMRINA-II §§1–4 = SOUND-AFTER-REPAIRS` may be promoted, subject to the three
   485	carried dependencies named below.  `DOMRINA-II-SOUNDNESS` as a whole
   486	**remains unpromoted**, and the reason has changed rather than disappeared:
   487	the blocker is no longer "two named gaps in the first half" but (i) §§5–7 are
   488	unaudited — including the forward consumers of Lemma 3.15, Lemma 7.10 and the
   489	omitted §7 arithmetic; (ii) the Domrina–Orevkov I inheritance is only
   490	partially bound, since campaign Proposition 4.1 replaces part I's defective
   491	unique-μ=1 inference and nothing else, so the "number of dicritical components
   492	is greater than 1" entry to Proposition 1.2 still rides part I's separate
   493	unique-μ=2 analysis, which no lane has re-audited; and (iii) the three
   494	structure packages (F1)/(F2) and (S1)/(S2)/(S4) are consumed, not re-derived.
   495	Anyone quoting this report should quote all three.
   496	
   497	**Effect on the N=4-LITERATURE-CLOSED reception line.**  Unchanged, and this
   498	matters more than the headline.  Repairing two first-half gaps does not make
   499	Domrina II a checked proof of the N=4 case; it makes the first half checked
   500	and the second half untouched.  `N=4-LITERATURE-CLOSED` therefore stays
   501	**NOT ASSERTED**.  What has changed is the shape of the residual risk: before
   502	this lane, a reader could reasonably have suspected that the paper's root
   503	ledger was structurally defective, in which case the whole route would have
   504	been in question; that suspicion is now retired, and the residual risk is
   505	localised in §§5–7 and in the part-I μ=2 inheritance.  The campaign's
   506	independent N=4 chain — the S₄ row-kill theorem, the six (8,6)/(9,6)
   507	AM-numerical types under exact msolve decision, and the ROW-NF exhaustiveness
   508	dependency that the closure review keeps labelled PROVISIONAL — remains the
   509	load-bearing path to B0 at N=4, exactly as before.  Nothing here strengthens
   510	or weakens it; the two efforts are independent, and it would be a mistake to
   511	let a repaired Domrina lemma relax the exhaustiveness obligation on the
   512	campaign side.  Conversely, had either implication turned out false, the
   513	campaign chain would have become the *only* live path; it did not, and I
   514	record that soberly: the honest summary is that a literature route which was
   515	in doubt is now, in its first half, in better shape than the campaign had
   516	assumed, and in its second half exactly as unknown as before.
   517	
   518	**One reusable asset.**  Lemma DET-LINF (`det L̃∞ ⩽ 0`) is proved here
   519	unconditionally from properness plus Hodge index plus Grauert contraction, and
   520	is stronger than anything in the paper.  It discharges a hypothesis that
   521	Domrina re-verifies case by case in §§5–7, so it is worth banking on its own
   522	account for the sibling lane auditing those sections.
