+# DOMRINA-INSTANTIATE — the repaired walk does not start on the residual alone
+
+**Lane:** `DOMRINA-INSTANTIATE`. **Desk-pass verdict:** outcome **(c),
+`NO-KILL / NOT-INSTANTIABLE`**. The proposed first fork is ill-typed as stated.
+Lemma 2.12 can force Domrina's distinguished **source-boundary root**
+`v~` into `Q1 union Q2`; it cannot force the `(9,6,2)` Puiseux/infinity datum,
+the infinity place of `D_1`, or the target curve `D_1` into those branches.
+The campaign residual does not supply the source-resolution tree in which
+`Q1,Q2,Q3` live, a selected vertex `a~`, `det Q3 > 0`, or inequality (2.13).
+`DET-LINF` supplies exactly one of those hypotheses and no route-to-state.
+
+This is not a counterexample to the checked Domrina chain. The live object is a
+curve/profile substrate satisfying necessary campaign constraints, not a
+degree-four Keller map. Domrina starts after such a map has supplied a morphism
+of compactifications and its source lattice. Conditional on a Keller extension
+of the residual, her repaired universal chain excludes the extension (modulo the
+declared structure packages); it does not thereby eliminate the realized curve
+as a curve. No single `(F*)/(S*)` package is localized, because no Fig. 11 row or
+Lemma-2.12 vertex is selected. The sharp escalation target is instead the missing
+bridge `OPEN[RESIDUAL-TO-DOMRINA-STATE]`.
+
+## 0. Custody, scope, and status changes
+
+The three frozen inputs were hashed before reading. All values matched the
+charge exactly:
+
+```text
+2ad20b4c37128533ef23e956c2921aeb70d830bd6166a11b95a6ef6637cc5eff  ideation-20260902T0022Z-fable5.md
+99fc1e5870fb74d48e3d14a156115ef625fa9ecbc5843f0d8dd4a138a920e9bf  domrina-gap-repair-opus5-20260901.md
+a47945ab0fdb8e8245f2ec03558eaafc0cab9b64bd4bbcd2c859afb370db2401  rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md
+```
+
+The repository copies have the same three hashes. The official Domrina II PDF
+is held under full SHA-256
+`0be24c5c6a9cc9423c3049c3402f2c98e44bac5f1c6018b3999989e0f32e5018`;
+that custody and the repair review's source use are recorded at
+`xmodel/domrina-repair-review-gpt55-20260901.md:12-21`. Per the charge, this
+lane performs one instantiation pass and does not re-verify the replayed
+sections.
+
+Two post-packet typings are carried rather than silently back-propagated.
+
+1. The hostile review of the part-I `mu=2` track confirmed all five charged
+   items and `DO-I-MU2 = REPLAYED-SOUND (+ named local repairs)`
+   (`xmodel/mu2-replay-review-grok46-20260902.md:8-23,404-455`). Thus the old
+   `PROVISIONAL` flag on that track is removed here. This does not remove the
+   Domrina `(F*)/(S*)` package boundary.
+2. The sibling Sol submission's argument `deg D_2 >= 3` is consulted only as
+   **`EXACT-DESK/UNREVIEWED`**. It excludes a conic via the immersion/embedding
+   gate and supplies a nodal cubic merely as a topology control, explicitly not
+   as attainment by a Keller map
+   (`xmodel/ideation-20260902T0022Z-sol56.md:98-110`). No stronger status is
+   assigned to that degree floor.
+
+No exit-price assertion is introduced. A `charge_basis` declaration is
+therefore inapplicable.
+
+## 1. Type the two sides before trying to join them
+
+### 1.1 What the campaign residual actually supplies
+
+The residual consists of three different layers, none of which is a source
+compactification.
+
+| layer | supplied datum | exact scope |
+|---|---|---|
+| carrier/owner budget | one nontrivial carrier `(mu,s,K)=(2,1,0)`, one trivial carrier `(1,1,0)` on a second owner, owner weights `(2,1)` (displayed unordered as `W=(1,2)`) | a budget/ownership profile, not a dual graph |
+| target curve `D_1` | the realized parametrized `(9,6,2)` curve, four affine nodes, one place at infinity with characteristic pair `(3;25)`, `delta_inf=24`, `M_inf=27` | target-curve geometry and infinity series |
+| companion `D_2` | necessary relation `chi_2+sigma_2=1`; degree floor `>=3` only at `EXACT-DESK/UNREVIEWED` status | normalization/topology and a degree floor, not a joint embedding or source lift |
+
+The carrier definition is `c=mu*s+K`, with owner weight the sum of `mu*s`
+over its carriers (`xmodel/reducible-all-n-r2-opus5-20260901.md:291-305`).
+At `N=4` the unique row is the `(2,1,0)` core plus one trivial on a second
+owner, `W=(1,2)`, but that report expressly says it recovers only the
+**budget/ownership projection**, not the cage itself
+(`xmodel/reducible-all-n-r2-opus5-20260901.md:424-432`). Consequently the word
+"core" does not encode an intersection lattice, a path, a root, or a
+compactification.
+
+For `D_1`, the frozen REP report derives
+
+```text
+Delta=(9,6,2),  S_aff=<2,9>,  delta_aff=4,
+beta_1=25,      delta_inf=24, M_inf=27.
+```
+
+It then verifies the explicit parametrization and its four nodes
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:59-84,109-141`). These are target
+series/place invariants. The same report finds only six classes of
+`rho_inf`-fixed `S_4` data and says that the type passes GATE-3; it does not
+produce a representation of the full complement group
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:483-518,740-743`). The full braid
+factorization remains the first missing object
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:607-641`).
+
+The reducible profile does require a second owner/component. In the frozen
+calculation its block-free Euler identity reduces to
+`chi_2+sigma_2=1`; the four nodes of `D_1` cancel and the equation constrains
+only the companion's normalization in that parametrization
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:688-708`). This equality does not locate
+the companion's infinity series relative to `D_1`, give the joint embedded
+resolution, or construct a map having `D_1 union D_2` as its nonproperness set.
+The frozen verdict still lists construction of `D_2` and the companion gate as
+open (`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:710-716`). Even granting a target
+curve witness would not supply the source tree below.
+
+### 1.2 What Domrina's symbols mean
+
+Domrina assumes a degree-four constant-Jacobian map and then resolves it to a
+regular morphism `F:X~ -> X` between compact smooth surfaces. Its source
+boundary is `L~`, `L~_infinity=F^{-1}(L)`, and the two source dicriticals are
+`g1~`,`g2~`, with restriction degree one and transverse orders one and two.
+The distinguished root `v~` is a vertex of `L~_infinity`. This map-level entry
+and the separation between dicritical components, physical infinity points,
+and transverse orders are summarized at
+`xmodel/domrina-1999-audit-sol56-20260901.md:82-102`.
+
+The repaired Lemma 2.12 has the following typed input/output:
+
+```text
+input:  a~ in <g1~ g2~> in the source tree L~;
+        Q1 = br_a~(g1~), Q2 = br_a~(g2~);
+        Q3 = the components of delta(g1~ g2~) incident to a~;
+        det L~_infinity <= 0;
+        det Q3 > 0;
+        det(a~ gi~) <= det(delta(a~ gi~))^2 det Q3 for i=1 or 2.
+
+output: v~ in Q1 union Q2.
+```
+
+This is the statement at
+`xmodel/domrina-gap-repair-opus5-20260901.md:121-135`. The unconditional
+`DET-LINF` proof supplies only `det L~_infinity <= 0`
+(`xmodel/domrina-gap-repair-opus5-20260901.md:141-176`). In particular:
+
+- `v~` is a source-lattice vertex, not the one place at infinity of `D_1`;
+- `Q1,Q2,Q3` are branches/subgraphs of `L~`, not Puiseux blocks or target
+  components;
+- `det(a~ gi~)` is a determinant of a declared source subgraph, not one of
+  `(9,6,2)`, `beta_1`, `delta_inf`, or `M_inf`;
+- `det L~_infinity <= 0` is a necessary sign after a suitable `F` and
+  compactification exist. It does not construct `F` or identify any branch.
+
+The numerical resemblance is therefore only a conditional interface hint:
+if an actual Keller extension realizes the campaign row with exactly one
+order-two and one order-one dicritical, one would expect the weight-two image
+`D_1` to carry the label `g_2` and the weight-one companion `D_2` the label
+`g_1`. Matching the numbers `2` and `1` does not prove this identification, and
+still less does it construct `g1~`,`g2~`, `L~`, or `v~`. The earlier campaign
+audit makes precisely this distinction: the residual has a conditional
+structural match to Domrina Proposition 1, but does not prove her
+compactification identity, target diagrams, or transverse boundary meetings
+(`xmodel/domrina-1999-audit-sol56-20260901.md:261-282`).
+
+## 2. The charged first fork
+
+The question "is the `(9,6,2)` infinity data forced into `Q1 union Q2` by
+Lemma 2.12 plus DET-LINF?" has answer **NO: the proposed membership is not
+well-typed**. The legally testable question would be:
+
+> After a Keller extension and compactification have supplied a selected
+> `a~`, its three branch sets, and the two remaining determinant hypotheses,
+> does Lemma 2.12 force the source root `v~` into `Q1 union Q2`?
+
+The answer to that conditional question is yes. The charged residual cannot
+instantiate its antecedent. The hypothesis audit is exact:
+
+| Lemma 2.12 obligation | supplied by the residual? | supplied by `DET-LINF`? | desk verdict |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| a morphism `F:X~ -> X` extending a degree-four Keller map | no | no | `OPEN[SOURCE-OPEN-U]` upstream |
+| source tree `L~`, root `v~`, dicritical vertices `g1~`,`g2~` | no | presupposed | not constructed |
+| selected `a~ in <g1~ g2~>` | no | no | no route-to-state |
+| definitions of `Q1,Q2,Q3` at that `a~` | no | no | undefined on the substrate |
+| `det L~_infinity <= 0` | only conditional on the missing map/state | yes, once that state exists | one hypothesis only |
+| `det Q3 > 0` | no | no | requires a source-branch proof/package |
+| inequality (2.13) for `i=1` or `2` | no | no | requires exact path determinants |
+| conclusion `v~ in Q1 union Q2` | not reached | Lemma 2.12, if all rows above hold | not a claim about `(9,6,2)` |
+
+Thus the first fork stops before either branch of the lemma's proof. It is not
+that the inequality was tested and failed, nor that the root was found in
+`Q3`. The vertex and determinants are absent. Filling them from the Puiseux
+tuple would violate both the flag/place/series guardrail and the
+target/arrival-state guardrail.
+
+## 3. One desk pass through the full chain
+
+The following is the complete pass. "Available" means supplied at its correct
+type; "conditional" means it follows only after assuming a Keller extension;
+"not reached" means no analogous target-curve value was substituted.
+
+| step | object/claim | result on the charged residual |
+|---:|---|---|
+| 0 | `N=4` budget row `(2,1,0)`, two owners, `W=(1,2)` | **available**, but only as budget/ownership projection |
+| 1 | realized `D_1=(9,6,2)` target curve | **available** with one infinity place and four nodes |
+| 2 | full local-braid-fixed `phi:pi_1(C^2-D_1)->S_4` | **OPEN**; only product-fixed classes are banked |
+| 3 | target pair `D_1 union D_2` as the actual nonproperness set of a map | **OPEN**; topology/degree constraints are not map attainment |
+| 4 | a source open `U isomorphic to A^2` in the finite cover, with the required etale map | **OPEN[SOURCE-OPEN-U]** |
+| 5 | compactifications and regular `F:X~->X`, minimal source boundary `L~` and root `v~` | **not constructed** |
+| 6 | Domrina Proposition 1.2 state and one of the ten Fig. 11 source diagrams | **conditional only**; no row selected by the residual |
+| 7 | a Lemma-2.12 vertex `a~`, `Q1,Q2,Q3`, positivity and (2.13) | **not reached** |
+| 8 | repaired R1/R2 root placement, followed by the relevant section 5, 6, or 7 terminal arithmetic | **not reached** |
+| 9 | Lemma 7.11 / no four-sheeted Keller map | **valid as the checked universal conditional theorem**, not a curve-level discriminator |
+
+There are two nested gaps, and keeping them separate matters. Step 2 is the
+frozen REP report's finite braid-factorization problem. Even a success there
+would produce a branched cover, not the Keller source; the frozen report names
+the source realization as its largest geometric gap
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:643-652`). Steps 4-5 are the later
+source-open/boundary-lattice bridge. The synthesis has already adopted the
+corrected target `OPEN[SOURCE-OPEN-U]`: the finite normalization is not itself
+`A^2`; one must find an open `U isomorphic to A^2` with typed boundary, then
+compactify it (`xmodel/ideation-20260902T0022Z-synthesis.md:22-58`).
+
+The exact parting point with Domrina is step 5. The campaign can state target
+component and cover constraints through step 4, but her `Q`-walk starts in the
+source compactification produced at step 5. There is no legal shortcut from the
+one Puiseux place to that source tree.
+
+## 4. What the repaired theorem would do after the missing bridge
+
+Assume, only for this paragraph, that the residual extends to a genuine
+degree-four Keller map and that its compactification satisfies Domrina's entry.
+Then the walk is universal rather than special to `(9,6,2)`:
+
+```text
+confirmed D-O-I mu2 inheritance
+  -> Proposition 1.2: two dicriticals of transverse orders 1 and 2
+  -> sections 1-3 degree/block machinery
+  -> Lemma 3.12: 35 local signatures
+  -> Lemma 3.14: ten Fig. 11 quotient graphs
+  -> cases 2a-2b: section 4 elimination
+     cases 1a-1d: section 5 elimination
+     cases 3a-3b: section 6 elimination
+     cases 4a-4b: section 7 elimination
+  -> Lemma 7.11
+  -> contradiction to the assumed Keller map.
+```
+
+The replay's exact case ledger and dependency graph are at
+`xmodel/domrina-ii-replay2-sol56-20260901.md:695-750`. R1, R2 and
+`DET-LINF` were then hostile-reviewed: R1/R1' and R2 are confirmed; the
+downstream-safe R2' form suffices; the still-open inessentiality at the fork is
+consumed nowhere in sections 5-7
+(`xmodel/domrina-repair-review-gpt55-20260901.md:26-55,238-345`). With the
+post-packet `mu2` confirmation, the remaining declared trust boundary is the
+structure packages, not the old part-I review flag.
+
+This conditional chain kills the **assumed map extension**. It cannot be used
+backwards to say that no parametrized curve with `Delta=(9,6,2)` exists: that
+curve is explicitly verified. Nor can it say that no target pair satisfies the
+campaign's necessary cage equations. The frozen REP report is explicit that no
+promoted gate kills `(9,6,2)` and that the missing objects stand between the
+substrate and a Keller map
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:710-716`). There is consequently no
+logical collision between the checked theorem and the live substrate.
+
+## 5. Structure-package localization fails before package choice
+
+For completeness, the packages retained by the repair are:
+
+- **Domrina `(F1)`**: every connected component of `F^{-1}(U_c)` used in R1 has
+  determinant one.
+- **Domrina `(F2)`**: at the selected vertex all but two source branches lie in
+  those lifted components; the two exceptional directions are the `h^0`
+  direction and a positive linear branch.
+- **Domrina `(S1)`**: `det delta(a~ g2~)>0` in the Lemma 3.15 configuration.
+- **Domrina `(S2)`**: every component of that delta outside `U^0` is linear.
+- **Domrina `(S4)`**: the only possible fork is `h~`, and its incident `U^0`
+  components have determinant one.
+
+Their statements and use are recorded at
+`xmodel/domrina-gap-repair-opus5-20260901.md:199-217,307-335`; the repair
+explicitly says they were consumed rather than re-derived
+(`xmodel/domrina-gap-repair-opus5-20260901.md:455-460`). `(S3)` is not in that
+remaining package set because it was independently reconstructed. These names
+must not be confused with the unrelated `(F1)`/`(F2)` filter labels in the
+campaign census.
+
+No one package can honestly be named **THE** target in this lane:
+
+1. The residual does not select a source Fig. 11 row. Target degree and Puiseux
+   data alone do not choose among classes 1a-1d, 2a-2b, 3a-3b, and 4a-4b.
+2. It does not select an R1 or R2 application vertex. Hence it cannot show that
+   the attempted kill first depends on `(F1)/(F2)` rather than
+   `(S1)/(S2)/(S4)`, or vice versa.
+3. The failure occurs before the hypotheses of either package are meaningful:
+   no source `F^{-1}(U_c)`, `delta(a~g2~)`, or `h~` has been constructed.
+
+Calling outcome (b) and choosing one package would therefore be arbitrary. The
+package boundary remains attached to the universal Domrina theorem, but it is
+not the instantiation blocker exposed here. The single sharp target generated
+by this pass is a bridge theorem/certificate, not a package re-review.
+
+## 6. Exact escalation target
+
+Open the following typed item:
+
+```text
+OPEN[RESIDUAL-TO-DOMRINA-STATE]
+
+Input:
+  a full braid-factorization survivor for D_1 union D_2;
+  a finite cover with the campaign sheet/owner data;
+  a declared Zariski-open U isomorphic to A^2 giving the Keller source.
+
+Required certificate:
+  (1) compactifications X~, X and a regular extension F:X~->X;
+  (2) the joint target resolution of D_1 union D_2 at infinity;
+  (3) the source boundary L~, L~_infinity, root v~, and dicriticals g1~,g2~;
+  (4) checked assignment D_2<->g1 and D_1<->g2, including transverse orders;
+  (5) a selected Fig. 11 row and route to a concrete a~;
+  (6) Q1,Q2,Q3 with det Q3>0 and the exact (2.13) inequality.
+
+Success:
+  invoke Lemma 2.12, the reviewed R1/R2 repairs, the selected section 5-7
+  terminal chain, and record the first F*/S* package actually consumed.
+
+Failure:
+  kill that cover/source-open realization; do not infer nonexistence of D_1.
+```
+
+This item is the operational version of the already-adopted boundary-lattice
+razor. The sibling Sol submission states the same fail-closed rule: missing
+cover-to-boundary landing data returns `OPEN`, never a tree inferred from a braid
+label (`xmodel/ideation-20260902T0022Z-sol56.md:84-94`). It is also the smallest
+object that would make Card C's desired package localization possible.
+
+The escalation is therefore precise. It is **not** "recheck all five Domrina
+packages" and not "the repaired proof disagrees with a realized curve." It is:
+the campaign currently lacks the route from its target residual to the source
+state on which the repaired proof operates. Until that bridge is produced,
+there is no concrete `Q1 union Q2` fork to run.
+
+## 7. Outcome and campaign ledger
+
+```text
+DOMRINA-FIRST-FORK
+  = NOT-INSTANTIABLE.
+    Lemma 2.12 would place v~, but (9,6,2) supplies no a~/Q-state.
+
+OUTCOME
