+| 9 | Lemma 7.11 / no four-sheeted Keller map | **`SOUND-AFTER-REPAIRS` relative to `(F1)/(F2)/(S1)/(S2)/(S4)`**, not a curve-level discriminator |
+
+There are two nested gaps, and keeping them separate matters. Step 2 is the
+frozen REP report's finite braid-factorization problem. Even a success there
+would produce a branched cover, not the Keller source; the frozen report names
+the source realization as its largest geometric gap
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:643-652`). Steps 4-5 are the later
+source-open/boundary-lattice bridge. The synthesis has already adopted the
+corrected target `OPEN[SOURCE-OPEN-U]`: the finite normalization is not itself
+`A^2`; one must find an open `U isomorphic to A^2` with typed boundary, then
+compactify it (`xmodel/ideation-20260902T0022Z-synthesis.md:22-58`).
+
+The earliest map-attainment breaks are already steps 2-4. The first interface
+specific to Domrina's state is step 5: the campaign can formulate the
+cover/source-open obligations but has not supplied their objects, while her
+`Q`-walk starts in the source compactification produced there. There is no legal
+shortcut from the one Puiseux place to that source tree.
+
+## 4. What the repaired theorem would do after the missing bridge
+
+Assume, only for this paragraph, that the residual extends to a genuine
+four-sheeted (`N=4`) Keller map, that its compactification satisfies Domrina's
+entry, and that the five declared structure-package inputs hold. Then the walk
+is universal rather than special to `(9,6,2)`:
+
+```text
+confirmed D-O-I mu2 inheritance
+  -> Proposition 1.2: two dicriticals of transverse orders 1 and 2
+  -> sections 1-3 degree/block machinery
+  -> Lemma 3.12: exhaustive local fork census (35 raw -> 16 surviving types)
+  -> Lemma 3.14: ten Fig. 11 quotient graphs
+  -> cases 2a-2b: section 4 elimination
+     cases 1a-1d: section 5 elimination
+     cases 3a-3b: section 6 elimination
+     cases 4a-4b: section 7 elimination
+  -> Lemma 7.11
+  -> contradiction to the assumed Keller map.
+```
+
+The replay's exact case ledger and dependency graph are at
+`xmodel/domrina-ii-replay2-sol56-20260901.md:695-750`. R1, R2 and
+`DET-LINF` were then hostile-reviewed: R1/R1' and R2 are confirmed; the
+downstream-safe R2' form suffices; the still-open inessentiality at the fork is
+consumed nowhere in sections 5-7
+(`xmodel/domrina-repair-review-gpt55-20260901.md:26-55,238-345`). With the
+post-packet `mu2` confirmation, the remaining declared trust boundary is the
+structure packages, not the old part-I review flag.
+
+This conditional chain kills the **assumed map extension**. It cannot be used
+backwards to say that no parametrized curve with `Delta=(9,6,2)` exists: that
+curve is explicitly verified. Nor can it say that no target pair satisfies the
+campaign's necessary cage equations. The frozen REP report is explicit that no
+promoted gate kills `(9,6,2)` and that the missing objects stand between the
+substrate and a Keller map
+(`xmodel/rep-96-inner-opus5-20260901.md:710-716`). There is consequently no
+logical collision between the checked theorem and the live substrate.
